WEBVTT

00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:07.148
-Get him out of there.
-Come on. Grab the end.

00:00:07.228 --> 00:00:08.268
(GEARS JAM)

00:00:08.588 --> 00:00:10.148
Are you okay?

00:00:10.228 --> 00:00:13.228
Can you hear me, Sharkbait?
Nemo? Can you hear me?

00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:14.748
Yeah, I can hear you.

00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:17.468
Sharkbait, you did it!

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:20.468
Sharkbait, you're...
Covered with germs!

00:00:20.588 --> 00:00:21.548
That took guts.

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:26.668
All right, we have less than
48 hours before Darla gets here.

00:00:26.748 --> 00:00:28.828
This tank will get plenty dirty
in that time,

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:31.068
but we have to help it along.

00:00:31.148 --> 00:00:33.628
-Jacques, no cleaning.
-I shall resist.

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:36.388
GILL: Everybody else,
be as gross as possible.

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:37.948
Think dirty thoughts.

00:00:38.028 --> 00:00:41.588
We're going to make this tank so filthy,
the dentist'll have to clean it.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.108
-(BURPS)
-Good work.

00:00:51.388 --> 00:00:53.948
All right, we're here, dudes.

00:00:54.028 --> 00:00:56.828
Get ready! Your exit's coming up, man.

00:00:56.908 --> 00:01:00.428
-Where? I don't see it.
-Right there. I see it. I see it.

00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:05.308
-You mean the swirling vortex of terror?
-That's it, dude.

00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:09.268
-Of course it is.
-First, find your exit buddy.

00:01:10.428 --> 00:01:13.548
-Do you have your exit buddy?
-Yes.

00:01:13.628 --> 00:01:19.028
Squirt here will now give you a rundown
on proper exiting technique.

00:01:19.148 --> 00:01:22.268
Good afternoon. We're going to have
a great jump today.

00:01:23.308 --> 00:01:26.468
Crank a hard cutback
as you hit the wall.

00:01:26.548 --> 00:01:29.468
There's a screaming bottom turn,
so watch out.

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:32.308
Remember, rip it, roll it and punch it!

00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.988
It's like he's trying to speak to me,
I know it.

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:40.748
You're really cute, but I don't know what
you're saying. Say the first thing again.

00:01:40.828 --> 00:01:43.828
Okay, Jellyman. Go, go, go!

00:01:51.508 --> 00:01:53.428
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.508
Whoo!

00:01:57.828 --> 00:01:59.748
That was fun.

00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:02.028
I actually enjoyed that.

00:02:02.108 --> 00:02:03.548
Hey, look! Turtles.

00:02:04.988 --> 00:02:06.508
Most excellent.

00:02:06.588 --> 00:02:12.108
Now, turn your fishy tails round and
swim straight on through to Sydney.

00:02:12.188 --> 00:02:13.748
No worries, man.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.428
No worries. Thank you, Dude Crush.

00:02:16.508 --> 00:02:18.748
-ALL: Bye.
-See you, Jellyman.

00:02:18.828 --> 00:02:21.108
Tell your little dude I said hi, okay?

00:02:21.188 --> 00:02:23.788
-See ya later, dudes.
-DORY: Bye, everyone.

00:02:24.308 --> 00:02:26.388
Nemo would have loved this.

00:02:27.268 --> 00:02:31.108
Hey, Crush. I forgot. How old are you?

00:02:31.188 --> 00:02:33.228
CRUSH: 150, dude!

00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:36.028
And still young. Rock on!

00:02:36.108 --> 00:02:39.388
150. I got to remember that.

00:02:40.348 --> 00:02:41.748
Whoa.

00:02:46.108 --> 00:02:48.628
-We going in there?
-Yep.

00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:50.628
P. Sherman, 42 Wallaby Way, Sydney?

00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:51.708
Yep.

00:02:52.628 --> 00:02:55.268
We're going to just swim straight.

00:02:56.548 --> 00:02:58.628
♪ Just keep swimming ♪

00:02:58.708 --> 00:03:00.188
MARLIN: Dory...

00:03:09.428 --> 00:03:11.988
MARLIN: Boy, this is taking a while.

00:03:12.068 --> 00:03:13.548
DORY: Hey, how about
we play a game?

00:03:13.628 --> 00:03:14.668
MARLIN: Okay.

00:03:14.748 --> 00:03:18.028
Okay, I'm thinking of something orange.

00:03:18.108 --> 00:03:19.948
-And it's small...
-It's me.

00:03:20.028 --> 00:03:21.028
Right.

00:03:21.108 --> 00:03:25.508
This one you'll never guess.
It's orange and small.

00:03:25.588 --> 00:03:26.628
It's me.

00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:28.588
All righty, Mr. Smarty Pants.

00:03:28.668 --> 00:03:31.868
It's orange and small
and white stripes...

00:03:31.948 --> 00:03:34.148
Me. And the next one, just a guess, me.

00:03:34.228 --> 00:03:35.388
Okay. That's just scary.

00:03:35.468 --> 00:03:38.548
Wait. I've seen
this floating speck before.

00:03:38.628 --> 00:03:41.228
That means we've passed it.

00:03:41.308 --> 00:03:43.628
That means we're not going straight.

00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:46.708
We got to get to the surface.
We'll figure it out there.

00:03:46.788 --> 00:03:47.948
-Hey!
-What?

00:03:48.028 --> 00:03:50.268
Relax. Take a deep breath.

00:03:53.948 --> 00:03:56.468
Now, let's ask somebody for directions.

00:03:56.548 --> 00:03:58.988
Fine. Who? The speck?
There's nobody here!

00:03:59.068 --> 00:04:01.548
There has to be someone.
It's the ocean.

00:04:01.628 --> 00:04:04.308
We're not the only two in here.
Let's see...

00:04:04.388 --> 00:04:06.188
Okay, no one there.

00:04:06.268 --> 00:04:07.708
Nope.

00:04:07.788 --> 00:04:09.268
Nada.

00:04:11.428 --> 00:04:14.228
-There's somebody. Hey, excu...
-Dory!

00:04:14.308 --> 00:04:16.748
I'm thinking of something mysterious.

00:04:16.828 --> 00:04:21.068
It's a fish we don't know, and if we
ask it directions, it could ingest us.

00:04:21.148 --> 00:04:23.588
What is it with men
and asking for directions?

00:04:23.668 --> 00:04:27.308
Don't play the gender card.
Let's play the "let's not die" card.

00:04:27.388 --> 00:04:29.348
-Want to get out of here?
-Of course.

00:04:29.428 --> 00:04:33.468
How are we going to do that unless
we give it a shot and hope for the best?

00:04:33.588 --> 00:04:36.668
-You don't fully understand.
-Trust me on this.

00:04:45.828 --> 00:04:47.268
All right.

00:04:49.308 --> 00:04:51.828
Excuse me? Little fella?

00:04:53.228 --> 00:04:54.268
Hello.

00:04:54.348 --> 00:04:56.228
Don't be rude. Say hi.

00:04:56.308 --> 00:04:57.948
Hello.

00:04:58.028 --> 00:05:00.348
-His son Bingo...
-Nemo.

00:05:00.428 --> 00:05:02.628
-...was taken to...
-Sydney.

00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:04.108
Sydney, yes.

00:05:04.188 --> 00:05:07.948
It's really important
that we get there as fast as we can.

00:05:08.028 --> 00:05:09.828
Can you help us out?

00:05:10.428 --> 00:05:13.428
Come on, little fella. Come on.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.708
Dory, I'm a little fella.

00:05:17.268 --> 00:05:20.028
I don't think that's a little fella.

00:05:22.548 --> 00:05:24.908
Big fella. Whale. Okay.

00:05:24.988 --> 00:05:27.108
Maybe he only speaks whale.

00:05:28.508 --> 00:05:30.988
(MOOING DRAWL) We need

00:05:31.068 --> 00:05:34.308
to find his son.

00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:37.188
What are you doing?
Are you sure you speak whale?

00:05:37.268 --> 00:05:40.268
Can you give us...

00:05:40.348 --> 00:05:43.348
-Heaven knows what you're saying.
-...directions?

00:05:43.428 --> 00:05:46.828
-MARLIN: See, he's swimming away.
-Come back.

00:05:46.908 --> 00:05:48.468
You've offended him.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:52.868
Maybe a different dialect. (MOOING)

00:05:53.428 --> 00:05:56.668
This is not whale.
You're speaking, like, upset stomach.

00:05:56.748 --> 00:05:59.388
-Maybe I should try humpback.
-No, don't.

00:05:59.628 --> 00:06:00.708
(GROWLING)

00:06:01.068 --> 00:06:03.668
-You sound sick.
-Maybe louder, huh?

00:06:03.748 --> 00:06:05.668
-Don't do that.
-Too much orca.

00:06:05.748 --> 00:06:10.548
-Didn't that sound a little orca-ish?
-It sounds like nothing I've ever heard.

00:06:10.628 --> 00:06:12.308
-(MOOING)
-(GROANS)

00:06:12.908 --> 00:06:14.668
Just as well. He might be hungry.

00:06:14.748 --> 00:06:17.708
Whales don't eat clownfish.
They eat krill.

00:06:17.788 --> 00:06:20.428
-KRILL: Swim away!
-Look. Krill!

00:06:23.388 --> 00:06:26.028
Move, Dory! Move!

